hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19042","Haddathana Hushaym, anbaana Hilal ibn Khabbab who said: Haddathani Maysara Abu Salih from Suwayd ibn Ghafala who said: The alms-collector of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us. He said: I sat with him and heard him saying: Indeed in my covenant is that I take nothing from a suckling milch animal, and what is separate is not to be gathered, nor what is gathered to be separated. And a man came to him with a tall she-camel, saying: Take it, but he refused to take it."
